(text "Source: upstream/gcwireless_bridge @ 5c31147 (https://github.com/heatherspacek/gcwireless_bridge).\nBoard: CMakeLists.txt sets no board, so the Pico SDK default (pico) applies; build-support/build-bridge.sh\npasses -DPICO_BOARD=pico. The SDK header boards/pico.h (SDK 2.1.1) defines the default SPI pins.\n\nGPIO  use                         source line\nGP27  joybus DATA to console      src/main.cpp:10  _pinTX = 27 ; enterMode(_pinTX, ...)\nGP16  SPI0 RX (data in)           src/main.cpp:87  PICO_DEFAULT_SPI_RX_PIN  (pico.h: 16)\nGP18  SPI0 SCK (clock in)         src/main.cpp:88  PICO_DEFAULT_SPI_SCK_PIN (pico.h: 18)\nGP19  SPI0 TX (data out)          src/main.cpp:89  PICO_DEFAULT_SPI_TX_PIN  (pico.h: 19)\nGP17  SPI0 CSn (chip select)      src/main.cpp:90  PICO_DEFAULT_SPI_CSN_PIN (pico.h: 17)\nGP25  onboard LED, set high       src/joybus.cpp:100 gpio_put(25, 1)\nSPI runs as peripheral, old term slave (src/main.cpp:86 spi_set_slave), 1 MHz setting, 10-byte reads (BUF_LEN = 10).\nPin numbers on the symbol are GPIO numbers; physical pin numbers were not checked." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 90.000 50.000 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)) (justify left top)) (uuid "fa867a7b-2879-5ff9-bb9e-c9358ee08d20"))
(embedded_fonts no)
)
